What steps can reproduce the bug?
Bun compares the SNI server name byte-for-byte when picking a per-hostname TLS context, so an SNI that differs only in case falls through to the default context. Node compiles each addContext() name into a case-insensitive RegExp:
$ node -e 'const s=require("tls").createServer({}); s.addContext("admin.example.com",{}); console.log(String(s._contexts[0][0]))'
/^admin\.example\.com$/i

