What steps can reproduce the bug?
Blob/File stores lastModified as an f64. The structured-clone deserialize path reads it as raw bytes and the .lastModified getter boxes it with JSValue::js_number(...) without purifying NaN. JSC's JSVALUE64 encoding is only sound for a non-NaN or the single canonical NaN; any other NaN bit pattern collides with the tag ranges for boolean, undefined, Int32, and cell pointers. So a structured-clone buffer — the untrusted input v8.deserialize(buffer) / bun:jsc.deserialize(buffer) is designed to take — can make .lastModified (a property that must always be a Number) decode as an arbitrary forged JSValue.
