SYNC THROW: HBOOM — the .catch never attaches, so a handled rejection becomes an uncaught synchronous exception. Any handler in Bun's own native option extraction (src/runtime/webcore/fetch.rs) that runs user JS via ?-propagation has the same shape: headers (an iterable/getter), and — after #29103's fix — proxy.url (a toString/Symbol.toPrimitive). Every validation failure in that same block already correctly builds a rejected promise; only genuine user-JS exceptions escape synchronously.
