Bun resolves web-worker to its browser shim. The web-worker package has a "bun" export condition pointing at src/browser/index.js, which is just:
export default typeof Worker !== 'undefined' ? Worker : undefined;
So new Worker(...) is Bun's native Web Worker, not Node's worker_threads wrapper.
ffjavascript hands the worker a data: URL. threadman.js base64-encodes the entire worker function into a data:application/javascript;base64,… string (~2.6 KB) and does new Worker(dataUrl).
