Description
The ES decorator proposal (tc39/proposal-decorators) specifies that member decorator expressions must be evaluated before class decorator expressions. Bun evaluates them in reverse order: class decorator factories are called first.
Reproduction
let counter = 0;

function dec1() {
  const n = counter++;
  return () => {};
}
function dec2() {
  const n = counter++;
  return () => {};
}
function dec3() {
  const n = counter++;
  return () => {};
}

@dec1()
@dec2()
class BugReport {
  @dec3() x: number = 20;
}

// Expected order (per spec): dec3 factory → dec2 factory → dec1 factory
// Actual order (Bun): dec1 factory → dec2 factory → dec3 factory
console.log("Expected: dec3=0, dec2=1, dec1=2");
console.log("counter =", counter);
Root Cause
src/js_parser/lower/lower_decorators.rs — Phase 8 (Assemble output) emits the class decorator array declaration (var _dec = [dec1, dec2]) before member decorator array declarations (var _dec2 = [dec3]). The arrays themselves are already built in Phase 2, but the order of emission determines evaluation order.
Fix: swap the emission order so member decorator arrays come first, then class decorator array.
Additional Related Failures
The same test file (test/bundler/transpiler/decorators.test.ts) has 12 failures total:

Evaluation order (6 tests): member vs class decorator factory order (root cause above)
target binding (4 tests): expect(target === A.prototype).toBe(true) receives false — decorator target is not the prototype
propertyKey serialization (1 test): String(propertyKey) produces "[object Object]" instead of the correct string key
export default class (2 tests): decorated methods not applied to default-exported classes

Issues 2-4 are separate bugs not fixed by the ordering change.

