Node's fsPromises.realpath is documented as using the same semantics as fs.realpath.native(), i.e. the native realpath(3) path. Its errors carry syscall: "realpath", and a trailing separator on a regular file is rejected with ENOTDIR (only the JS walking implementation behind fs.realpath/fs.realpathSync ignores trailing separators).
