{"code":"ENOTDIR","syscall":"lstat"}

Bun routes fs.promises.realpath to the non-native (emulated) variant: src/js/node/fs.promises.ts wraps the binding's realpath, which src/runtime/node/node_fs_binding.rs maps to RealpathNonNative. Node routes fsPromises.realpath to the native binding. The visible symptom today is the wrong syscall tag on every error. Once #32920 lands (it teaches the non-native variant to ignore trailing separators, matching Node's realpath/realpathSync), fs.promises.realpath("<file>/") will also resolve on Bun where Node rejects with ENOTDIR, because promises.realpath rides on the variant that change is correcting.
Additional information
The likely fix is routing fs.promises.realpath to the native binding (realpathNative) in src/js/node/fs.promises.ts. It is cross-platform (it also changes which Windows arm of realpath_inner runs, and which variant src/js/internal/fs/glob.ts uses internally for its async path), so it was kept out of #32920, which is a POSIX-only fix for the non-native variant. Filing separately so it is tracked.

