toEqual is documented to ignore undefined properties when comparing objects. The matcher expect.arrayContaining([expected]).toEqual(actual) honours this on plain objects, and on frozen flat objects. It stops honouring it as soon as the outer object is Object.freezed and carries a property whose value is another object. The extra key: undefined on actual is then flagged as a diff.
The inner object does not need to be frozen — only the outer.
import { expect, test } from "bun:test";

