Additional information
Root cause: Use-after-free race in onAbort. When the response body is an async ReadableStream, the await in pull yields the event loop. If a client disconnects during that yield, onAbort fires and tears down the stream's internal sink structures while the async pull resumption is still pending — both paths mutate/free the same memory.
