The spawn failure is silently swallowed: the child appears to have run and produced empty output. With some binaries (e.g. git) we even observed exit code 0 with empty stdout, which is indistinguishable from a successful child that printed nothing. The threshold is exactly fd 10240 — a pipe fd of 10239 works, 10240+ fails (binary-searched).
Additional information
How we hit this in practice: invoking bun test with an un-rooted path argument (e.g. bun test packages/daemon/src/foo.test.ts, no leading ./) puts bun in filter mode, which scanned our monorepo (~22k files) and held ~11.6k directory fds while tests executed. Any test that then called spawnSync with piped stdio got pipe fds >= 10240 and silently lost the child's output — 6 of our tests failed on "empty git worktree list output" with no error surfaced anywhere, and the failures vanished when the same file was invoked with a rooted ./ path. Linux is unaffected.
Two related issues here:

The posix_spawn failure should surface as an error (as node's EBADF does) instead of empty stdout — this is the main ask; the silent variant cost us days of debugging.
bun test filter mode retains the repo-scan directory fds during test execution, which is what pushes pipe fds above 10240 in the first place.

