// input:  6 lines (including blanks)
// output: 3 lines  ← interfaces + adjacent blanks dropped
console.log(input.split('\n').length, '→', out.split('\n').length);
There's no way for a downstream tool to map output line 2 back to input line 5 without re-implementing TS parsing.
