When a native socket closes, Bun pushes null to the readable stream but never calls destroy() on the socket. If the readable side is paused or the writable was never ended, autoDestroy never fires. The socket stays in a zombie state (_handle=null, destroyed=false), server._connections never decrements, and server.close() hangs forever.
