Bug Description
When a RedisClient connection drops and auto-reconnects, the in_flight promise queue is not cleared. Stale promise entries from the old connection remain in the FIFO queue, causing subsequent responses on the new connection to be resolved against the wrong promises.
This results in commands receiving responses that belong to entirely different commands — e.g., redis.get() resolving with "OK" (a SET response) instead of the actual value or null.
Steps to Reproduce

Create a singleton RedisClient with default options (enableAutoPipelining: true, enableAutoReconnect: true)
Issue concurrent Redis commands from multiple request handlers sharing the same client
Trigger a transient connection drop (e.g., Redis restart, network blip, cloud networking hiccup)
After auto-reconnect, observe that responses are mismatched to the wrong callers

Minimal reproduction:
import { RedisClient } from "bun";

const redis = new RedisClient("redis://localhost:6379");
await redis.connect();

// Simulate concurrent usage from multiple request handlers
async function handler(id: number) {
  const key = `test:${id}`;
  await redis.set(key, `value-${id}`);
  const result = await redis.get(key);

  if (result !== `value-${id}`) {
    console.error(`MISMATCH: expected "value-${id}", got "${result}"`);
  }
}

// If a connection drop + reconnect occurs during concurrent execution,
// responses will be matched to wrong promises
await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: 100 }, (_, i) => handler(i)));
Root Cause
In src/valkey/valkey.zig, the onClose handler has three paths:

Manual close → calls fail() → rejects all in_flight + queue entries ✅
Auto-reconnect disabled → calls fail() → rejects all entries ✅
Auto-reconnect enabled → sets is_reconnecting = true, calls reconnect() → does NOT touch in_flight ❌

// valkey.zig:468-508
pub fn onClose(this: *ValkeyClient) bun.JSTerminated!void {
    this.unregisterAutoFlusher();
    this.write_buffer.clearAndFree(this.allocator);

    if (this.flags.is_manually_closed) {
        try this.fail(...);  // Rejects in_flight + queue ✅
        return;
    }
    if (!this.flags.enable_auto_reconnect) {
        try this.fail(...);  // Rejects in_flight + queue ✅
        return;
    }

    // Auto-reconnect path: in_flight is NOT cleared ❌
    this.retry_attempts += 1;
    // ...
    this.flags.is_reconnecting = true;
    this.flags.is_authenticated = false;
    this.onValkeyReconnect();
}
After reconnect, onOpen clears write_buffer and read_buf

