This is binary data corruption: bytes change during parsing (4 -> 3 bytes).
The same multipart payload parsed by Node's Fetch/Request implementation preserved all bytes in local control checks.
Request.formData() should preserve file bytes exactly; truncation at 0x00 violates expected Web API behavior.

What is the expected behavior?
The server receives all 4 bytes unchanged.
What do you see instead?
The server receives only 3 bytes: [31, 139, 8].
Additional information
This affects PocketBun file-upload compatibility because it depends on Bun's native multipart parser for Request.formData().
