The four logical properties should map to four distinct physical properties (for LTR):

border-start-start-radius → border-top-left-radius
border-start-end-radius → border-top-right-radius
border-end-start-radius → border-bottom-left-radius
border-end-end-radius → border-bottom-right-radius

What do you see instead?
All four properties are mapped to border-top-left-radius (LTR) / border-top-right-radius (RTL). The border-bottom-* variants are never emitted:
.box:not(:is(:lang(ae), :lang(ar), ...)) {
  border-top-left-radius: var(--r, 20px);
  border-top-left-radius: var(--r, 20px);
  border-top-left-radius: var(--r, 20px);
