  border-top-right-radius: var(--r, 20px);
  border-top-right-radius: var(--r, 20px);
  border-top-right-radius: var(--r, 20px);
  border-top-right-radius: var(--r, 20px);
}
The same border-top-left-radius is repeated four times instead of producing four different corner properties. This means elements render with rounded corners only on top, flat on the bottom.
Additional information
This is related to #25785 which was fixed in #26006. That PR fixed the VendorPrefix initialization so logical properties are no longer silently dropped, but the logical-to-physical property mapping itself is still incorrect —
border-end-start-radius and border-end-end-radius are being mapped to the same physical properties as border-start-start-radius and border-start-end-radius.
The bug only manifests when values contain var() references. With static values like 20px, Bun collapses all four into the border-radius shorthand and the incorrect mapping is avoided.
