I have a specific usecase where disallowing certain names from being removed during treeshaking is necessary. I'm using TypeScript to write games on TIC-80 and since manual reloads are a drag, I've been cooking up a workflow for hot reloading. It's basically functional otherwise, but the biggest hurdle is that Bun (and any other bundler I've tested so far) has no way of keeping specific functions in the bundle when they are not exported. TIC-80 uses functions like TIC, BOOT, etc. as global handlers that are to be defined for the system. These must exist in the bundle for the program to work, but can't be exported or manually put into a global scope in the script to prevent being omitted.
The usecase is that I have some development only utility functions I need while developing, but I want to eject from the production build to concerve space and improve performance. For example a very naive example would look like this:
