Bun's node:http2 client has two flow control bugs that cause streams to permanently hang when receiving more than 65,535 bytes:

initialWindowSize in SETTINGS is ignored — the server never sees the client's requested window size. With Node.js the server sees remoteWindowSize=10485760; with Bun it sees remoteWindowSize=65535 (the default).
WINDOW_UPDATE frames are never sent — after the default 65,535-byte window is exhausted, the client never replenishes it, so the server stalls permanently.

