// Shows: react -> ../../@types+react@19.2.7/node_modules/@types/react ✗
TypeScript fails:
cd packages/lib-react18 && bunx tsc --noEmit
What is the expected behavior?

@types/react should resolve per-workspace based on each workspace's declared version, matching how the runtime react package resolves correctly
packages/lib-react18 specifies @types/react@^18.3.27, so transitive dependencies like @ariakit/react should resolve their type imports to @types/react@18
TypeScript should see consistent React 18 types across all imports in lib-react18
bunx tsc --noEmit should pass without type errors

What do you see instead?

@types/react is hoisted to .bun/node_modules/@types/react pointing to @types/react@19.2.7
Transitive dependencies like @ariakit/react resolve their type imports through this hoisted symlink, getting React 19 types
TypeScript sees a mismatch: lib-react18 uses React 18 types, but @ariakit/react uses React 19 types
